---
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { getPage } from "../lib/site";

const page = getPage("/terms");
---
<Base title={page.title} description={page.description} path={page.path}>
  <PageHead
    title="Terms of use"
    lead="These terms cover your use of kalcoded.com and the KalCode early-access list."
  >
    <p class="muted small">Last updated September 24, 2026</p>
  </PageHead>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>1. About these terms</h2>
      <p>
        By using kalcoded.com (the “site”) or joining the early-access list, you agree to these
        terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the site. The KalCode desktop application is
        not yet available; it will be offered under its own terms when it is released.
      </p>

      <h2>2. The site</h2>
      <p>
        The site describes KalCode, a product in private development. Descriptions of features,
        plans and prices reflect current plans and may change before release. Nothing on the site is
        an offer to sell, and no purchase can be made through it today.
      </p>

      <h2>3. The early-access list</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Joining is free and requires only an email address that you are entitled to use.</li>
        <li>
          Joining does not guarantee access to any build, on any date, and does not create an
          account or any other obligation for you or for us.
        </li>
        <li>
          We will use your address only as described in the <a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a>.
          You can remove it at any time on that page.
        </li>
        <li>Pre-release builds, if offered, may come with additional terms that you will see first.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>submit an email address that is not yours, or submit addresses in bulk;</li>
        <li>attempt to disrupt, overload, probe or bypass the security of the site or its API;</li>
        <li>scrape the site in a way that degrades it for others;</li>
        <li>use the site to break any law.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Names and marks</h2>
      <p>
        KalCode, JARVIS as used within KalCode, the KalCode wordmark and the constellation globe
        artwork are ours. You may not use them in a way that suggests endorsement or affiliation
        without permission. Claude Code, Codex and Gemini CLI are products and trademarks of their
        respective owners; naming them describes compatibility and does not imply endorsement.
      </p>

      <h2>6. No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided “as is” and “as available”. To the extent the law allows, we make no
        warranties about the site, including that it will be uninterrupted or error-free, or that
        KalCode will be released in any particular form or on any particular date.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental or
        consequential loss arising from your use of the site or the early-access list. Nothing in
        these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. When we do, we will change the date at the top of this page.
        Continuing to use the site after an update means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        A contact address for legal and privacy requests will be published on this site once a
        monitored mailbox is in place. Until then, you can remove your email address at any time
        with the form on the <a href="/privacy#remove">privacy page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
